\description{
Scan each pixel's class sequence across a named list of classified rasters
(one per year) and report whether it is \strong{stable}, a \strong{clean switch} (class
A for N years, then class B for M years, and nothing else) or \strong{flicker}
(more than one change of class). A clean switch is dated. This is the
temporal, categorical-only leg of change QA: where
\code{\link[=dft_transition_artifact]{dft_transition_artifact()}} asks whether a patch has the \emph{shape} of a
registration artifact and \code{\link[=dft_rast_break]{dft_rast_break()}} asks whether the \emph{spectral}
